  "query_preview": "/Saturday through Wednesday/...\nA large trough will move on shore and across the Pacific Northwest \nand Northern Rockies this weekend. This will bring a significant \ncooling trend that will drop daytime temperatures to 10-15 degrees \nbelow normal by Sunday along with breezy to windy conditions in \nnorthwest flow. Not much precipitation is expected from this system. \nSaturday night and Sunday probability of precipitation is around a \n30-50 percent over the northernmost mountain areas of our forecast \narea, including McCall, and about 20-30 percent for high terrain \nacross the south. Snow levels will lower to about 4000-5000 feet. \nFrom Monday through Wednesday of next week, our area will mostly \nstay under a dry west-northwest flow with temperatures trending up \nto near seasonal normals.",
